// Title: Linux Shell Pipe to Shell
// Sigma ID: 880973f3-9708-491c-a77b-2a35a1921158
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-03-14 | Modified: 2022-07-26
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1140
// Description: Detects suspicious process command line that starts with a shell that executes something and
//   finally gets piped into another shell
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software that uses these patterns
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_susp_pipe_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine startswith "sh -c " or ProcessCommandLine startswith "bash -c ") and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "| bash " or ProcessCommandLine contains "| sh " or ProcessCommandLine contains "|bash " or ProcessCommandLine contains "|sh ") or (ProcessCommandLine endswith "| bash" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "| sh" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "|bash" or ProcessCommandLine endswith " |sh"))
